WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.380
Everyone has bad dreams, whether they’re
about unconscious memories, showing up to

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.680
school in your underwear, or a man in a stripy
sweater with a spiky glove and a serious moisturizing

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:17.220
problem Nightmares are never far from us,
a common occurrence as part of the human experience,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.440
and they can happen to anyone.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:24.619
Of course, working for the SCP Foundation
means being faced with actual nightmares - not

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:28.320
only in the middle of the night - but on a
day-to-day basis.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.430
Giant, unkillable lizards with pure hatred
for humanity, ancient eldritch beings with

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:38.980
enough cosmic power to wipe out entire dimensions,
and a species of busses with gigantic insect

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.520
legs that feed on human beings.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.270
Needless to say, the researchers and operatives
that find themselves employed by the SCP Foundation

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:51.440
come face to face with some pretty horrific
creatures, enough to give anyone sleepless

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.440
nights.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:58.270
This naturally begs the question: What could
possibly scare the workers of the SCP Foundation?

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:01.010
What could the Foundation possibly have nightmares
about?

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:08.189
Well, they don’t really have a name for
him, just a designation: SCP-990.

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:12.880
Multiple members of Foundation staff have
all made reports of witnessing the same entity.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.619
After all, when you deal with dangerous cognitohazards
for a living, it’s worth taking every unusual

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:23.119
occurrence seriously, instead of just relying
on the old “it’s just a dream” excuse.

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:26.960
Anyone from doctors and research personnel,
to Mobile Task Force operatives and those

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.189
working as anomaly-guarding security - every
person working for the Foundation is at risk

00:01:32.189 --> 00:01:35.880
of an unwanted encounter with SCP-990.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.759
The reports are all consistent, they all describe
a man, seemingly a human being.

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:44.739
This figure always seems to appear dressed
in a business suit, but not like you might

00:01:44.739 --> 00:01:48.579
see a modern CEO or a Wall Street stockbroker
wearing.

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:53.810
Instead, SCP-990’s sense of fashion seems
to be at least a few decades out, and he seems

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:58.169
to favor wearing clothing more in line with
the style of the Cold War era.

00:01:58.169 --> 00:01:59.759
Wait, that can’t be it, right?

00:01:59.759 --> 00:02:03.679
The big bad boogeyman that terrorizes the
dreams of the SCP Foundation’s staff is

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:05.719
just… a man in a suit?

00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:07.799
What is he, an IRS Agent?

00:02:07.799 --> 00:02:12.360
Well, while SCP-990 might not be all that
scary to look at when compared to other frightening

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:17.219
anomalies like the haunting beaked visage
of the Plague Doctor, or the unknowable horror

00:02:17.219 --> 00:02:22.420
that is SCP-096, it’s not the way he looks
that’s terrifying.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.510
It’s the ominous warnings he carries with
him.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:29.420
What is interesting is that, while most dreams
are usually our brains’ way of processing

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:35.480
our memories or real-world experiences and
anxieties, SCP-990 seems to have no recorded

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.700
existence beyond what has been reported by
staff.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:44.290
He seems to exclusively exist within the dreams
of Foundation personnel, with absolutely none

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:49.140
of these people having witnessed or encountered
the suit-wearing man in the real world.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.260
If there is, somewhere out there among the
seven billion people on Planet Earth, a man

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:59.019
who resembles SCP-990, then the Foundation
has been unsuccessful in tracking him down.

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:02.779
What’s more, is that there has never been
a single report from outside of the Foundation

00:03:02.779 --> 00:03:07.670
– not one civilian or even any member of
another Group of Interest – that anyone

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:11.620
else has ever had a dream involving SCP-990.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:16.120
For years now he’s been cropping up exclusively
in the nightmares of Foundation personnel,

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:19.860
but was first discovered a number of years
ago after several agents began to discuss

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:24.890
the fact that they had all experienced similar
dreams, all revolving around a mysterious

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.790
man in a Cold War-era business suit.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:33.879
But then, he finally became known to the higher-ups
at the Foundation after one peculiar incident.

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:38.799
An agent had failed to report to his assigned
post at the right time, and from that moment

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:42.590
on, things would never be the same again.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:46.620
After scouring the Foundation facility for
this missing agent, when fellow members of

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.159
personnel found him, he was fast asleep in
his quarters.

00:03:50.159 --> 00:03:52.689
Doesn’t seem too unusual right?

00:03:52.689 --> 00:03:57.469
After all, working at the SCP Foundation has
got to be pretty hard going, with some horrendous

00:03:57.469 --> 00:04:02.189
overtime hours, so maybe the agent just needed
to catch up on some sleep by taking a quick

00:04:02.189 --> 00:04:04.139
nap before the start of his shift.

00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:07.959
Then again, eighteen whole hours is one hell
of a long nap.

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:12.870
That’s right, the man had been unconscious
for eighteen hours.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:17.209
When they found him, fellow Foundation staff
were unable to awaken the sleeping agent,

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:20.660
his body having entered some form of short-term
coma.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.250
Unsure if he would ever wake again, medical
personnel had the agent moved to the sick

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:30.520
bay on-site, where he was placed under surveillance
and continued his long sleep.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:36.250
After almost two whole days, and an uninterrupted
forty-hour period of sustained sleep, the

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.810
agent finally awoke.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:42.699
He was agitated, erratic - Clearly, something
had rattled him pretty severely.

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:46.740
The agent dashed out of his bed in the medical
bay and began frantically running through

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:51.080
the corridors of the Foundation facility,
screaming and babbling about the impending

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.460
end of the entire world.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:57.690
Eventually, medics were able to restrain the
man, injecting him with powerful sedatives

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.420
to relax him long enough for them to secure
him.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:04.840
Yet somehow, the agent’s bodily functions
remained in a heightened state even after

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:09.750
he was sedated; his heart was beating at a
dangerously accelerated rate and his blood

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:12.310
pressure was spiking to quite an alarming
degree.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:16.900
Now, we might not be medical experts, but
we can guarantee that high blood pressure

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:20.509
and an elevated heart rate are rarely ever
good signs.

00:05:20.509 --> 00:05:25.479
Then again, neither is being asleep and unable
to wake up for forty solid hours.

00:05:25.479 --> 00:05:30.770
As you may have already guessed, when he finally
calmed down, the agent described a dream that

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:34.639
revolved around a man dressed in a business
suit that seemed to match the styles of the

00:05:34.639 --> 00:05:36.050
Cold War era.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.949
In other words, SCP-990.

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:42.759
But you see, it’s not like the mysterious
man trapped the agent in this forty-hour dream

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:44.270
just to torture him.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:47.879
There was no pulling the agent through the
center of his mattress causing a volcanic

00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:50.810
eruption of blood to splatter up to the ceiling.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:56.130
SCP-990 didn’t wrap any bed sheets around
the agent’s neck, or slash at him using

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.420
a glove with a blade at the end of each finger.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:05.259
Instead, all SCP-990 did during the course
of the agent’s dream was deliver a message.

00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:09.319
Well, actually it was more of a warning than
anything else.

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:14.020
After he had awoken and calmed down from his
prior outburst, the agent was being evaluated

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.000
by a Foundation doctor.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.770
During this evaluation, the agent was able
to describe, in the most acute, precise detail

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.580
imaginable, a chilling sequence of events.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:30.520
Something that was so accurate that it could
only have been true, instead of just an inconsequential

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.190
dream, or a fabricated, made-up story.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:37.889
The agent was describing exactly how the world
was going to end.

00:06:37.889 --> 00:06:42.819
Not a single detail was omitted, the exact
times and dates, the tipping of every domino

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:47.310
on the geopolitical landscape that would ultimately
lead to annihilation.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:52.530
SCP-990 had appeared in the agent’s dream
to describe exactly how, at some point in

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:59.129
time, a series of events would culminate in
multiple tactical nuclear warheads being launched.

00:06:59.129 --> 00:07:03.409
These deadly weapons of mass destruction would
head straight for targets in Central Europe

00:07:03.409 --> 00:07:07.850
and eastern Asia, seeming to imply that the
missiles were to be launched by the United

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:09.449
States of America.

00:07:09.449 --> 00:07:13.690
The resulting devastation of the nuclear payload
would wipe out almost the entirety of the

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:19.009
human race, exterminating around ninety-eight
percent of the planet’s population.

00:07:19.009 --> 00:07:24.080
Society would collapse on a global scale,
and the world would be rendered a barren,

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:28.569
inhospitable wasteland ravaged by radioactive
fallout.

00:07:28.569 --> 00:07:34.540
Every detail of this impending apocalypse
was relayed to the agent by SCP-990, including

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:40.120
exactly who and what would trigger the initial
chain of events destined to end in total destruction

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.160
of Earth.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:46.060
Deciding to take the mysterious suited man’s
message seriously, the SCP Foundation dispatched

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:50.840
one of its elite Mobile Task Forces to eliminate
that initial threat, removing the thing that

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:52.789
would topple the first domino.

00:07:52.789 --> 00:07:57.889
While the crisis was averted, and the world
saved, the agent who first reported his encounter

00:07:57.889 --> 00:08:03.130
with SCP-990 died, suffering symptoms resembling
severe shock.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:07.140
Of course, just because you manage to stop
one approaching apocalypse, doesn’t mean

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:08.360
that there won’t be others.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:12.900
In fact, when you think about it, that’s
the scariest thing about SCP-990.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:18.850
It’s not that he appears in Foundation personnel’s
dreams, it’s that his work is never done.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:23.930
He always brings with him a new warning of
a new disaster on the horizon.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:28.979
If anything, the ripples caused by preventing
one of these crises only create another to

00:08:28.979 --> 00:08:30.189
deal with.

00:08:30.189 --> 00:08:37.130
Since this initial incident, now designated
as Event-990-07, SCP-990 has made a number

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:41.900
of similarly ominous warnings through the
nightmares of other members of the SCP Foundation.

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:47.160
Any one of this business suit-wearing omen’s
warnings come with an almost one hundred percent

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.420
certainty rate.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:53.140
He can foresee the future without any margin
of error, successfully predicting the exact

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:58.270
dates, times, and causes of the deaths of
multiple doctors working for the Foundation.

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:03.510
Even the destruction of a noted facility,
known as Watch Station Epsilon 38, was foretold

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:06.540
by an appearance of SCP-990.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:11.670
Of course, theories about who or what exactly
this man is are common, but with no clear,

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.490
definitive answer to speak of.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:17.910
It’s currently up in the air if this entity
is some sort of guardian angel, helping the

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:23.320
SCP Foundation protect humanity from their
own downfall and guiding us all to safety.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:27.580
Or he could be a visitor from an infinite
number of potential futures, projecting himself

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:31.560
back in time to avert whatever course of action
led to the end of the world.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:36.590
The staff at the SCP Foundation are encouraged
to come forward if they ever have a nocturnal

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:42.100
encounter with SCP-990, with one doctor even
believing that the man has a physical body

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.120
somewhere out there in the real world.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:50.540
During one dream with SCP-990 in it, a Foundation
doctor was able to conduct a complete interview

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:51.540
with the man.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.720
Now, we all know that it can be pretty tricky
to recall the details of a dream after waking

00:09:55.720 --> 00:10:00.070
up, but this particular doctor claimed to
have an almost impeccable memory.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:05.760
It’s unclear how exactly this doctor was
able to converse so clearly with SCP-990,

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:10.310
but with so many people working for the Foundation,
perhaps it was only a matter of time before

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:13.940
the man in the suit found one capable of lucid
dreaming.

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:18.970
At the commencement of this dream interview,
when asked for his name, SCP-990 responded

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:22.290
with ‘Tony’, as if he had pulled the name
from thin air.

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:27.440
When the doctor asked if this was his real
name, SCP-990 claimed that a person should

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.310
have the right to be called whatever they
wish to be called, before changing his mind

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.410
and asking to be called Richard instead.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:38.810
The doctor pressed on, asking the man why
he had been delivering threats to Foundation

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:41.040
personnel through their dreams.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.540
SCP-990 seemed confused by this.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:47.840
Then, the doctor rebutted by accusing the
dream walker of murdering the agent, the one

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.390
who had first reported his encounter with
SCP-990.

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:55.750
Hearing this, the entity explained that the
Foundation had the wrong impression of him,

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.820
claiming he wasn’t the bad guy.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:02.740
Upon mention of a ‘bad guy’ being involved,
the doctor’s next course of action was naturally

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.640
to ask who this might be.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:11.990
And then SCP-990 said something even stranger:
it was the designation of another SCP.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:16.570
But not one that the Foundation had ever encountered
before, there didn’t even exist any anomaly

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.440
under the number that the mysterious dream
man had given.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:23.760
“There is no SCP with that designation,
and there won't be for some time,” the doctor

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.430
argued, growing ever more confused and agitated.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:29.160
“Well of course not,” SCP-990 replied.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:33.380
“She hasn't even been born yet, much less
classified by your Foundation.”

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:37.440
When asked if this was another prediction
of an impending disaster, yet another threat

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:44.130
that could end the entire world, SCP-990 simply
told the doctor “This is your wake-up call.”

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:48.660
Since then, no one is certain who or what
this future anomaly could be, whether she

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:52.680
has since been contained by the Foundation
or if that is still yet to come.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:57.930
The sad part about our dreams is they only
ever really offer us a look backwards, memories

00:11:57.930 --> 00:12:01.430
and experiences all warped in our sleeping
brains.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:05.940
None of us can look forward, nobody knows
exactly what the future holds.

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:09.780
Well, none of us except SCP-990, that is.

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:14.680
It’s been a long time since the Foundation
designated SCP-990.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:19.020
If that prophesied nightmare of an SCP has
been born and designated since then, what

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:20.300
do you think she is?

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.440
Let us know down in the comments.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:28.680
Now go check out “SCP-3017 - The Most Dangerous
Person Alive” and “SCP 1440 - The Old

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:33.490
Man That Kills All Living Things He Touches”
for more eerie humanoid SCPs!

